from __future__ import annotations

NAME = "Europa, the Ocean Moon"
AMBIENCE = "Whale Song"

# A soothing sleep-lecture about a smooth shell of ice over a hidden global ocean of salty water.
SECTIONS = [['You have nowhere to be right now.', 'There is nothing left for you to do tonight.', 'You can let your shoulders soften and sink a little deeper.', 'Let your eyes close, gently, with no effort at all.', 'Feel the weight of your body settling into the bed beneath you.', 'There is no need to hold anything anymore.', 'Breathe in slowly, and let the breath out even more slowly.', 'With each breath, you grow a little heavier, a little calmer.', 'Let your thoughts grow soft and slow, like clouds passing far away.', 'And as you settle, imagine yourself beginning to float, gently upward and outward.', 'You are drifting toward something far away, quiet, icy, and smooth.', 'A pale white moon, hanging silent in the dark, waiting calmly for you.'], ['Far from here, around the great planet Jupiter, this little moon turns quietly in the dark.', 'Its name is Europa, and it is one of the four large moons Galileo first saw, long ago in the year sixteen ten.', 'Through his small telescope, he watched these tiny lights circle Jupiter, night after patient night.', 'Europa is one of the smoothest worlds anyone has ever found.', 'It is wrapped, all the way around, in a shell of pale water ice.', 'From far away, it shines softly, like a smooth pearl resting in the blackness.', 'There are almost no mountains here, no jagged peaks reaching up.', 'Just a wide, gentle, frozen surface, calm and even in every direction.', 'It is very, very cold here, colder than anything you have ever known.', 'And yet there is a deep stillness to it, a quiet that feels almost peaceful.', 'Picture that smooth white world turning slowly, slowly in the dark.', 'Let your breathing slow to match its gentle, unhurried turning.'], ['Across the bright ice, long lines stretch for thousands of miles.', 'They are reddish brown, like faint streaks drawn across a pale page.', 'Scientists call these lines the lineae, the cracks in the frozen shell.', 'They cross over one another in soft curves, weaving a quiet pattern over the whole moon.', 'No one drew them, and yet they trace a kind of map across the ice.', 'In some places, the ice has broken into great rafts that drifted and settled again.', 'They call this the chaos terrain, though it rests now in perfect silence.', 'Imagine these pale rafts of ice, frozen mid drift, held still forever.', 'The whole surface looks young, with very few craters marking it.', 'That tells us the ice renews itself, slowly healing over the long ages.', 'Something beneath the surface keeps it smooth and fresh and new.', 'Let that thought settle softly over you as you breathe out once more.'], ['And now we come to the secret that Europa quietly holds.', 'Beneath that thick shell of ice, scientists believe there is an ocean.', 'A vast, dark, global ocean of liquid salty water, wrapping the whole moon.', 'It may hold twice as much water as all the oceans of Earth combined.', 'Think of that, an ocean larger than every sea you have ever imagined.', 'It is hidden away under many kilometres of solid ice, in total darkness.', 'No sunlight reaches it, no wind stirs it, no waves break upon any shore.', 'It simply rests there, deep and dark and endlessly calm.', 'How can water stay liquid so very far from the warmth of the sun?', 'Jupiter pulls and flexes the little moon as it circles, and that gentle squeezing makes warmth inside.', "They call this tidal heating, a slow warmth born from Jupiter's quiet, steady pull.", 'And so the hidden ocean stays soft and liquid, held safe beneath its ceiling of ice.'], ['Picture that ocean now, silent under a quiet sky of ice.', 'Nothing hurries there, in all that gentle dark.', 'The water is calm, holding everything within it with patient ease.', 'Long ago, a spacecraft named Galileo journeyed all the way to Jupiter.', 'It passed by Europa again and again, listening and watching from afar.', 'From what it found, scientists began to picture this ocean we now imagine.', 'And one day, perhaps, we will send another visitor to look more closely still.', 'Some people wonder, softly and with hope, what such an ocean might hold.', 'Wherever there is water and a little warmth, life sometimes finds a way.', 'No one knows, and that is part of the quiet wonder of it.', 'It is only a gentle question, drifting in the dark, asking nothing of you.', 'You can hold that little hope lightly, and let it carry you toward rest.'], ['So much of Europa is stillness, and stillness is a kind of peace.', 'A smooth white shell, turning slowly in the cold and quiet.', 'Beneath it, a dark ocean, patient and undisturbed, asking for nothing.', 'There is no rush there, no noise, no need to be anywhere else.', 'It has waited like this for billions of years, calm and unhurried.', 'And it will keep its quiet long after this night has passed.', 'There is something deeply restful in a calm that lasts so long.', 'You do not have to understand it all, you only have to rest within it.', 'Let the image of that silent ocean hold you for a moment.', 'Feel how peaceful it is, this hidden, gentle, sleeping sea.', 'Your breath is slow now, soft and even, like the calm of that deep water.', 'Let yourself drift a little closer to the edge of sleep.'], ['Now imagine you are sinking, slowly and softly, down through the calm dark water.', 'You pass gently beneath the smooth ceiling of ice, into the quiet below.', 'Here it is warm and dark and endlessly peaceful, and you are held by the water.', 'You weigh nothing at all now, floating, drifting, carried without any effort.', 'There is nothing to reach for, nowhere to go, only this gentle sinking down.', 'Down and down, into the soft and silent deep, you slowly drift.', 'Every part of you grows heavy and warm and wonderfully calm.', 'The quiet wraps all around you, holding you safe and still.', 'Your breathing is slow, your body is soft, your mind is drifting away.', 'Let the dark water carry you the rest of the way into rest.', 'There is nothing left to do now but sink gently into sleep.', 'Rest now, held in the calm, and drift softly away.']]
